166
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:42,880
We have two crew members that sit in the back

167
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:45,000
of the aircraft, and they're predominantly crew chiefs

168
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:46,200
and door gunners.

169
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:49,300
And they assist with the loading and unloading of the aircraft.

170
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:52,140
We're a utility helicopter, so we want to get in and get out.

171
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,440
And the door guns are predominantly there to assist

172
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:57,340
in the suppression of the enemy and provide area coverage.

173
00:08:57,341 --> 00:09:00,940
The UH-60M Black Hawk helicopter is the successor

174
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:05,280
to the old UH-1 Huey from the Vietnam War.

175
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:07,880
The Hueys became the workhorses of the military,

176
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:11,380
and much like the Black Hawks, filled many different roles.

177
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:14,720
They evacuated wounded soldiers, transported troops,

178
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:19,000
dropped supplies, and were even used as gunships.

179
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,140
But while the Huey pilots flew using only visual references

180
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:25,640
on the ground and maps, Black Hawk pilots

181
00:09:25,641 --> 00:09:29,520
Black Hawk pilots fly with state-of-the-art instruments.

182
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:32,040
This aircraft really takes the technology we have

183
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:34,040
in the civilian sector and moves Army aviation

184
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,380
into the 21st century.

185
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,620
It really does two things.

186
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,580
It increases our situational awareness

187
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:40,620
so that when we have the moving map displays,

