on down the assembly line, getting its electrical harness

516
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:20,800
installed, its gearbox is put in, and the engine is installed.

517
00:26:20,900 --> 00:26:23,300
After the helicopter is completely assembled,

518
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:25,700
it's painted, flight tested, and ready for the customer

519
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:26,800
to fly at home.

520
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:32,440
Robinson's simple design allowed the company

521
00:26:32,441 --> 00:26:36,440
to produce nearly 900 helicopters in 2008 at its manufacturing

522
00:26:36,441 --> 00:26:38,580
facility in Torrance, California.

523
00:26:38,581 --> 00:26:41,280
No helicopter manufacturer had ever produced that many

524
00:26:41,281 --> 00:26:43,280
in a single year.

525
00:26:43,281 --> 00:26:45,780
Of course, they cost a little more now.

526
00:26:45,781 --> 00:26:55,200
The R-22 sells for $243,000, and the R-44 for nearly $400,000.

527
00:26:55,201 --> 00:26:58,900
One agency that realizes the value of a Robinson helicopter

528
00:26:58,901 --> 00:27:01,840
is the El Monte, California Police Department.

529
00:27:01,841 --> 00:27:05,340
They maintain a fleet of three R-44 helicopters that have

530
00:27:05,341 --> 00:27:07,940
been converted for police use.

531
00:27:07,941 --> 00:27:11,280
You have a high candle power searchlight, which is used

532
00:27:11,281 --> 00:27:13,780
to illuminate the ground person at night.

533
00:27:13,781 --> 00:27:17,280
We also have the FLIR, which is the forward-looking infrared,

534
00:27:17,281 --> 00:27:21,500
which enables the observer to see heat signatures on the ground

535
00:27:21,501 --> 00:27:23,100
at night and even during the day.

536
00:27:23,101 --> 00:27:26,240
We also have a different radio package, which allows us

537
00:27:26,241 --> 00:27:28,740
to talk to a wide variety of police agencies

538
00:27:28,741 --> 00:27:30,700
within the Los Angeles County.

539
00:27:30,701 --> 00:27:33,160
And there's other equipment, such as LoJack,

540
00:27:33,260 --> 00:27:36,940
which is a vehicle locating device.

541
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:38,840
Even with these extra add-ons,

542
00:27:38,940 --> 00:27:41,440
Robinson helicopters operate for a third of the cost

543
00:27:41,540 --> 00:27:46,140
of larger, more expensive police helicopters.

544
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:49,060
That allows us to have three, and it allows us

545
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:51,760
to stay in business and do what we do best,

546
00:27:51,860 --> 00:27:54,620
and that's providing a safe aerial platform

547
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:57,060
and a safe environment for the citizens we serve.

548
00:28:00,700 --> 00:28:02,660
Having that helicopter in the sky

549
00:28:02,760 --> 00:28:05,540
is equivalent to having anywhere from five to eight ground

550
00:28:05,640 --> 00:28:08,140
officers in the area, and also gives the police

551
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,440
a significant advantage.

552
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:19,660
The police pilot relies on ground communication

553
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:21,660
to get the helicopter into the right position.

554
00:28:24,960 --> 00:28:27,360
Once he locates the fleeing suspect,

555
00:28:27,460 --> 00:28:29,420
the co-pilot or tactical flight officer

556
00:28:29,421 --> 00:28:32,420
directs the ground forces.

557
00:28:32,520 --> 00:28:35,960
He will also monitor the FLIR system and searchlight at night

558
00:28:36,060 --> 00:28:39,060
until the suspect is apprehended.

559
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:41,960
Regardless of how much time and effort is put forth

560
00:28:42,060 --> 00:28:43,860
in trying to escape from the police officers,

561
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:45,860
they already know that the helicopter's there.

562
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:47,380
They're going to go to jail eventually.

563
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:51,780
You can run, but you're only going to go to jail tired.

564
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:54,020
But police departments aren't the only organizations

565
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:57,920
taking advantage of Robinson Helicopter's low costs.

566
00:28:57,921 --> 00:29:01,420
We have other versions of that same basic helicopter,

567
00:29:01,520 --> 00:29:04,420
which are used for TV broadcasts,

568
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:07,420
so the TV stations can buy that particular model,

569
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:10,760
and all the equipment for their gyro-stabilized cameras

570
00:29:10,860 --> 00:29:13,760
and microwave transmissions are all built right

571
00:29:13,860 --> 00:29:17,080
into the basic helicopter.

572
00:29:17,180 --> 00:29:19,580
These helicopters end up flying for industries

573
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:21,180
all over the world.

574
00:29:21,280 --> 00:29:25,020
About 70% of all of the helicopters that we manufacture

575
00:29:25,120 --> 00:29:26,480
are exported.

576
00:29:26,481 --> 00:29:28,480
exported all over the world.

577
00:29:28,580 --> 00:29:31,020
And some of our most active markets right now

578
00:29:31,120 --> 00:29:35,820
are places like South Africa, Australia, New Zealand,

579
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:37,920
and, of course, all of the European countries.

580
00:29:40,820 --> 00:29:42,600
The Robinson fills an important niche

581
00:29:42,700 --> 00:29:44,400
in an economically cautious world.

582
00:29:47,100 --> 00:29:49,340
But if you've got the money, you might prefer one

583
00:29:49,440 --> 00:29:50,840
of these tricked out choppers.

584
00:29:56,480 --> 00:30:00,420
Helicopters aren't just for police forces and the military.

585
00:30:00,520 --> 00:30:02,520
Some individuals and corporations

586
00:30:02,620 --> 00:30:06,420
like the luxury of commuting as the crow flies.

587
00:30:06,520 --> 00:30:09,720
For that, many people turn to Bell helicopters.

588
00:30:09,820 --> 00:30:13,100
We offer any helicopter for any need,

589
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:16,060
whether that's corporate or VIP travel to and from the golf

590
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:17,600
course and the boardroom.

591
00:30:17,700 --> 00:30:19,540
Any of our products in our line currently

592
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:21,700
can suit any of those needs.

593
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:26,480
Once you decide on a helicopter, Edwards and Associates

594
00:30:26,481 --> 00:30:29,920
It's Bell's completion house of choice.

595
00:30:30,020 --> 00:30:32,420
Edwards and Associates takes a Bell helicopter

596
00:30:32,520 --> 00:30:36,120
like this right off the line and customizes it

597
00:30:36,220 --> 00:30:38,520
from the inside out.

598
00:30:38,620 --> 00:30:40,220
When a customer wants to buy an aircraft,

599
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:43,160
the first thing we need to know is what kind of configuration

600
00:30:43,260 --> 00:30:44,260
do they need?

601
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:45,260
Is it corporate?

602
00:30:45,360 --> 00:30:46,960
Is it utility, VIP?

603
00:30:47,060 --> 00:30:49,040
Just what type of equipment do they need?

604
00:30:49,140 --> 00:30:52,540
We figure out what would best suit their mission requirements,

605
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:56,480
and then we build the aircraft from that proposal.

606
00:30:56,481 --> 00:31:02,120
And that can be costly, up to $2 million just for customizing.

607
00:31:02,220 --> 00:31:04,480
It starts with an 800-mile flight from Bell's

608
00:31:04,580 --> 00:31:05,580
manufacturing plant.

609
00:31:08,620 --> 00:31:10,820
Using only a basic instrument panel,

610
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:13,740
the helicopters make their way from Maribel, Canada,

611
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:16,940
to a facility in Piney Flats, Tennessee.

612
00:31:17,040 --> 00:31:19,840
This is what we start with when we begin our completion.

613
00:31:19,940 --> 00:31:22,040
It's what we call a green aircraft.

614
00:31:22,140 --> 00:31:23,940
It has no avionics, nothing installed,

615
00:31:23,941 --> 00:31:29,280
just the bare bones aircraft. Edwards disassembles the

616
00:31:29,281 --> 00:31:32,580
helicopter to start the customizing process.

617
00:31:32,581 --> 00:31:35,520
The helicopter then goes into the completions hangar, where

618
00:31:35,521 --> 00:31:38,680
workers install the wiring and flight instruments.

619
00:31:38,681 --> 00:31:41,800
Avionics installation is done in this facility.

620
00:31:41,801 --> 00:31:46,100
This aircraft is probably about 30% into the customizing at

621
00:31:46,101 --> 00:31:48,340
this point. We have begun to install all

622
00:31:48,341 --> 00:31:51,740
the wiring and all the equipment. One piece of high

623
00:31:51,741 --> 00:31:54,740
equipment going into this helicopter is what's known as a

624
00:31:54,741 --> 00:31:58,140
glass cockpit. This puts about five gauges

625
00:31:58,141 --> 00:32:00,940
into these two panels, and they're redundant, so if one

626
00:32:00,941 --> 00:32:04,220
fails, you have the backup on the bottom.

627
00:32:04,221 --> 00:32:06,780
The glass cockpit, as opposed to the traditional analog

628
00:32:06,781 --> 00:32:10,300
instruments, is just one of the avionics options that customers

629
00:32:10,301 --> 00:32:14,860
can choose. Their choices also include GPS,

630
00:32:14,861 --> 00:32:20,140
3D map displays, and even an advanced warning system.

631
00:32:20,141 --> 00:32:24,480
It gives you warnings if you're getting close to aircraft or

632
00:32:24,481 --> 00:32:27,840
antennas. Workers run wiring through the

633
00:32:27,841 --> 00:32:30,780
helicopter to connect the instrument panel in the front to

634
00:32:30,781 --> 00:32:33,060
the computer systems that control it placed in a rear

635
00:32:33,061 --> 00:32:36,320
compartment. After we finish the installation

636
00:32:36,321 --> 00:32:39,200
of the avionics and all the wiring and we buttoned up all

637
00:32:39,201 --> 00:32:43,100
the panels, this is when we start to install the interior.

638
00:32:43,101 --> 00:32:46,500
Customizing the interior starts with a plastic trim kit

639
00:32:46,501 --> 00:32:48,960
that will cover any wiring or equipment that was previously

640
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:51,500
installed.

641
00:32:51,600 --> 00:32:53,100
Next comes carpet.

642
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:55,440
And if you don't want a solid color,

643
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:58,440
we can have something such as this or this.

644
00:32:58,540 --> 00:33:01,040
All we got to do is get your design that you want,

645
00:33:01,140 --> 00:33:02,740
have a computer rendering done of it,

646
00:33:02,840 --> 00:33:05,720
and sent to the carpet company where they can manufacture it,

647
00:33:05,820 --> 00:33:08,760
whatever your logo is, however you want it to look.

648
00:33:08,860 --> 00:33:11,160
The seat covers come with the same options.

649
00:33:11,260 --> 00:33:13,460
Once the customer has chosen the colors and materials

650
00:33:13,461 --> 00:33:17,660
for the seats, they're handmade and installed.

651
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:19,260
The next step is plating.

652
00:33:19,360 --> 00:33:21,760
We have several examples here of some plating.

653
00:33:21,860 --> 00:33:22,760
Here's some door trim.

654
00:33:22,860 --> 00:33:25,100
This goes around where you open the door.

655
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:27,700
There's hundreds of colors of plating, different styles,

656
00:33:27,800 --> 00:33:29,880
brushed aluminum, brushed gold, whatever

657
00:33:29,980 --> 00:33:31,120
you would like to have.

658
00:33:31,220 --> 00:33:34,120
We put reclining seats in, had cabinets up

659
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:36,820
where they could talk on the phone or work on their laptop,

660
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:39,420
had monitors that actually would rise up.

661
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:40,560
The sky is the limit.

662
00:33:40,660 --> 00:33:42,860
Anything you want to do.

663
00:33:42,861 --> 00:33:44,520
But they aren't finished yet.

664
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:46,200
The last step is the paint.

665
00:33:46,300 --> 00:33:48,700
And this is where the customer can really make the helicopter

666
00:33:48,800 --> 00:33:49,700
his or her own.

667
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:57,100
In just four months, the workers at Edwards and Associates

668
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:59,340
take a helicopter straight off the line

669
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:01,340
and turn it into a hovering luxury suite.

670
00:34:03,880 --> 00:34:05,820
For those that can't afford an Edwards conversion,

671
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:06,720
there's still hope.

672
00:34:06,721 --> 00:34:11,720
Rotorway International in Chandler, Arizona,

673
00:34:11,820 --> 00:34:14,360
manufactures experimental helicopter kits

674
00:34:14,460 --> 00:34:15,900
that deliver to your door.

675
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,960
An experimental helicopter is a helicopter

676
00:34:19,060 --> 00:34:23,440
that is within easy reach of anybody to purchase,

677
00:34:23,540 --> 00:34:27,140
and it allows them to build the helicopter themselves.

678
00:34:27,240 --> 00:34:29,780
It also allows them to invest their time

679
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:32,780
and save exponential dollars.

680
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:35,340
Rotorway's two-seat A600 Talon

681
00:34:35,341 --> 00:34:41,340
is just over $100,000, some assembly required.

682
00:34:41,440 --> 00:34:44,980
It can fly as fast as 100 miles per hour.

683
00:34:45,080 --> 00:34:48,580
It can reach a ceiling height of approximately 8,000

684
00:34:48,680 --> 00:34:53,760
to 10,000 feet, and it is designed to give everyone

685
00:34:53,860 --> 00:34:56,100
the satisfaction of flying in a helicopter.

686
00:34:56,200 --> 00:34:59,800
We think that anybody can build this helicopter.

687
00:34:59,900 --> 00:35:03,460
RotorWay tries to make it easy on the garage mechanic.

688
00:35:03,461 --> 00:35:06,100
They assemble some of the more complex components for the

689
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:10,760
customer, including the drive assembly, tail boom,

690
00:35:10,860 --> 00:35:13,500
and most importantly, the engine.

691
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:17,300
We will send you a proven, dyno-tested, ready-to-install

692
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:18,600
engine for your helicopter.

693
00:35:21,420 --> 00:35:23,640
One man that knows all about building a rotorway

694
00:35:23,740 --> 00:35:27,520
helicopter is flight instructor Chris Strachan, who's building

695
00:35:27,620 --> 00:35:31,380
his third A600 Talon at his hangar in Van Nuys, California.

696
00:35:31,480 --> 00:35:32,660
It's a very simple process.

697
00:35:32,661 --> 00:35:34,500
They do most of the difficult stuff,

698
00:35:34,501 --> 00:35:36,660
and it's this 49%, 51% rule.

699
00:35:36,661 --> 00:35:40,160
The 49% that they do is all the difficult stuff,

700
00:35:40,161 --> 00:35:42,660
and then the other 51% is you just putting bolts together

701
00:35:42,661 --> 00:35:44,160
and brackets and actually putting together.

702
00:35:44,161 --> 00:35:46,160
It's almost like you just need your normal tools

703
00:35:46,161 --> 00:35:47,160
that you have in your backyard.

704
00:35:47,161 --> 00:35:49,660
That's pretty much all you need.

705
00:35:49,661 --> 00:35:52,160
Here at the factory, we make the parts cards

706
00:35:52,161 --> 00:35:53,660
where we take each part that you need,

707
00:35:53,661 --> 00:35:56,660
put it on the parts card, laminate it,

708
00:35:59,660 --> 00:36:01,660
put it in your crate.

709
00:36:02,660 --> 00:36:05,260
and you're good to go.

710
00:36:05,261 --> 00:36:07,900
Each parts card has a specific label on them

711
00:36:07,901 --> 00:36:10,660
with on your blueprints, explains to you exactly

712
00:36:10,661 --> 00:36:12,540
where each part needs to go.

713
00:36:12,541 --> 00:36:14,700
What I really like is rather than getting a box of bolts,

714
00:36:14,701 --> 00:36:16,580
they kind of shrink wrap them onto the card,

715
00:36:16,581 --> 00:36:19,300
each bolt with a number exactly where it goes.

716
00:36:19,301 --> 00:36:21,540
As a first-time builder, we supply you

717
00:36:21,541 --> 00:36:23,220
with construction manuals and videos,

718
00:36:23,221 --> 00:36:26,340
which take you step-by-step through each phrase.

719
00:36:26,341 --> 00:36:27,860
Then it's up to the customer.

720
00:36:27,861 --> 00:36:32,660
First step, order stage one of four shipments of crates.

721
00:36:32,661 --> 00:36:36,260
The customer then decides when to receive the next shipment.

722
00:36:36,261 --> 00:36:39,800
When you are ready for stage two of your helicopter kit,

723
00:36:39,801 --> 00:36:43,540
it will include some very high-end components, which

724
00:36:43,541 --> 00:36:47,180
are the drive and main drive systems and the body.

725
00:36:47,181 --> 00:36:49,940
The main drive system is a very intricate part

726
00:36:49,941 --> 00:36:54,420
of the helicopter, and that is the second step you will take.

727
00:36:54,421 --> 00:36:56,280
The drive assembly is what links the engine

728
00:36:56,281 --> 00:36:58,220
to the rotor blades.

729
00:36:58,221 --> 00:37:02,360
The helicopter begins to take shape at this stage.

730
00:37:02,361 --> 00:37:11,260
Once you receive group three, that will include your tail rotor system, some of your main drive pulleys, your oil system, and your engine cooling system.

731
00:37:11,700 --> 00:37:16,000
Four will include your engine, your rotor blades, and your ignition system.

732
00:37:16,001 --> 00:37:21,780
Once you receive this final stage, you will pretty much be able to complete your helicopter.

733
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:27,580
Rotorway says the average builder takes 400 to 650 hours to complete his helicopter.

734
00:37:28,980 --> 00:37:30,500
Rotorway monitors each stage.

735
00:37:30,501 --> 00:37:34,500
We will not allow you to go to the next stage of your build

736
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:37,640
until we feel confident that you've reached the goal

737
00:37:37,740 --> 00:37:40,640
or accomplished what we are asking you to accomplish

738
00:37:40,740 --> 00:37:43,240
before the next stage is taken on.

739
00:37:43,340 --> 00:37:45,840
Once the helicopter is completely built,

740
00:37:45,940 --> 00:37:48,160
it still can't be flown.

741
00:37:48,260 --> 00:37:51,660
The customer must contact a local FAA representative

742
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:53,660
and have them look over the helicopter.

743
00:37:55,760 --> 00:37:58,800
They will take you through a sign-off procedure

744
00:37:58,801 --> 00:38:00,960
where they will inspect your helicopter.

745
00:38:01,060 --> 00:38:03,440
Be sure it's built correctly.

746
00:38:03,540 --> 00:38:06,880
Finally, it's given an airworthiness certificate.

747
00:38:06,980 --> 00:38:10,320
Then the owner is free to fly his brand new helicopter.

748
00:38:10,420 --> 00:38:12,040
Most people don't realize that.

749
00:38:12,140 --> 00:38:14,080
For the price of a good Corvette,

750
00:38:14,180 --> 00:38:17,920
I can have a helicopter that can fly pretty much anywhere.

751
00:38:18,020 --> 00:38:20,320
Why even drive somewhere where you can fly?

752
00:38:20,420 --> 00:38:25,200
So perhaps you, too, will be flying a helicopter soon.

753
00:38:25,300 --> 00:38:28,800
But don't try this for your close-ups, your best.

754
00:38:28,801 --> 00:38:29,800
You'll want one of these.

755
00:38:36,340 --> 00:38:39,540
Today, not all helicopters have a pilot inside.

756
00:38:39,541 --> 00:38:42,720
Take the fire scout from Northrop Grumman.

757
00:38:42,721 --> 00:38:44,540
It's linked to a ground control facility

758
00:38:44,541 --> 00:38:47,520
that will give it coordinates.

759
00:38:47,521 --> 00:38:50,620
Once programmed, it can fly to an assigned area,

760
00:38:50,621 --> 00:38:54,420
perform its mission, and return home.

761
00:38:54,421 --> 00:38:57,460
It can even autonomously take off from and land

762
00:38:57,461 --> 00:39:01,260
aircraft carrier.

763
00:39:01,360 --> 00:39:04,940
Northrop Grumman modified a full-sized Schweitzer 333

764
00:39:05,040 --> 00:39:07,700
to create the Fire Scout.

765
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:11,940
It has a top speed of 145 miles per hour.

766
00:39:12,040 --> 00:39:14,380
Although the original intent was to use the Fire Scout

767
00:39:14,480 --> 00:39:16,440
to provide reconnaissance, it can

768
00:39:16,540 --> 00:39:19,280
be outfitted with rocket launchers and laser-guided missiles.

769
00:39:22,260 --> 00:39:24,560
The Fire Scout is certainly a successful pilotless

770
00:39:24,660 --> 00:39:27,060
helicopter, but in the future, perhaps

771
00:39:27,061 --> 00:39:31,060
helicopters will look and behave more like this one.

772
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:33,800
It's called the Dragonflyer X-6.

